      {
        "title": "Nephite Decline and Downfall",
        "slug": "downfall",
        "description": "After the visit of Jesus Christ, all the people live in a harmonious  Utopia. After 200 years of this Zion, corruption begins to creep into  the society again. Some people break away from the main body of people,  and identify themselves as Lamanites. The organized criminal ring of  Gadianton is revived, and the society begins the decline. A man named  Mormon is entrusted with the Nephite records and abridges the Nephite  history on a new set of gold plates. Mormon subsequently becomes the  military commander of the Nephites. Tensions grow between the Nephites  and Lamanites, and after several decades of intermittent war and peace,  the two nations gather near a hill called Cumorah and engage in a climactic  battle to end all battles. The Nephite nation is nearly entirely wiped  out, and Mormon’s son, Moroni, one of the last Nephite survivors, adds  to his father’s record, and hides the plates, in hopes that someday  they will be discovered.",
